            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Most JDBC drivers provide improved performance if you batch multiple calls to the same prepared statement. By grouping updates into batches, you limit the number of round trips to the database."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You accomplish "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JdbcTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " batch processing by implementing two methods of a special interface, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BatchPreparedStatementSetter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and passing that implementation in as the second parameter in your "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "batchUpdate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method call. You can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "getBatchSize"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method to provide the size of the current batch. You can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "setValues"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method to set the values for the parameters of the prepared statement. This method is called the number of times that you specified in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "getBatchSize"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " call. The following example updates the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "t_actor"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " table based on entries in a list, and the entire list is used as the batch:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "public class JdbcActorDao implements ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;\n\n\tpublic void setDataSource(DataSource dataSource) {\n\t\tthis.jdbcTemplate = new JdbcTemplate(dataSource);\n\t}\n\n\tpublic int[] batchUpdate(final List<Actor> actors) {\n\t\treturn this.jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = ?, last_name = ? where id = ?\",\n\t\t\t\tnew BatchPreparedStatementSetter() {\n\t\t\t\t\tpublic void setValues(PreparedStatement ps, int i) throws SQLException {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tActor actor = actors.get(i);\n\t\t\t\t\t\tps.setString(1, actor.getFirstName());\n\t\t\t\t\t\tps.setString(2, actor.getLastName());\n\t\t\t\t\t\tps.setLong(3, actor.getId().longValue());\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tpublic int getBatchSize() {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn actors.size();\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t});\n\t}\n\n\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "class JdbcActorDao(dataSource: DataSource) : ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate val jdbcTemplate = JdbcTemplate(dataSource)\n\n\tfun batchUpdate(actors: List<Actor>): IntArray {\n\t\treturn jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = ?, last_name = ? where id = ?\",\n\t\t\t\tobject: BatchPreparedStatementSetter {\n\t\t\t\t\toverride fun setValues(ps: PreparedStatement, i: Int) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tps.setString(1, actors[i].firstName)\n\t\t\t\t\t\tps.setString(2, actors[i].lastName)\n\t\t\t\t\t\tps.setLong(3, actors[i].id)\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t\toverride fun getBatchSize() = actors.size\n\t\t\t\t})\n\t}\n\n\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you process a stream of updates or reading from a file, you might have a preferred batch size, but the last batch might not have that number of entries. In this case, you can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "InterruptibleBatchPreparedStatementSetter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface, which lets you interrupt a batch once the input source is exhausted. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "isBatchExhausted"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method lets you signal the end of the batch."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jdbc-batch-classic",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Basic Batch Operations with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JdbcTemplate"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Both the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JdbcTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "NamedParameterJdbcTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " provides an alternate way of providing the batch update. Instead of implementing a special batch interface, you provide all parameter values in the call as a list. The framework loops over these values and uses an internal prepared statement setter. The API varies, depending on whether you use named parameters. For the named parameters, you provide an array of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SqlParameterSource"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", one entry for each member of the batch. You can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SqlParameterSourceUtils.createBatch"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " convenience methods to create this array, passing in an array of bean-style objects (with getter methods corresponding to parameters), "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "String"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "-keyed "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Map"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " instances (containing the corresponding parameters as values), or a mix of both."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example shows a batch update using named parameters:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "public class JdbcActorDao implements ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate NamedParameterTemplate namedParameterJdbcTemplate;\n\n\tpublic void setDataSource(DataSource dataSource) {\n\t\tthis.namedParameterJdbcTemplate = new NamedParameterJdbcTemplate(dataSource);\n\t}\n\n\tpublic int[] batchUpdate(List<Actor> actors) {\n\t\treturn this.namedParameterJdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = :firstName, last_name = :lastName where id = :id\",\n\t\t\t\tSqlParameterSourceUtils.createBatch(actors));\n\t}\n\n\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "class JdbcActorDao(dataSource: DataSource) : ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate val namedParameterJdbcTemplate = NamedParameterJdbcTemplate(dataSource)\n\n\tfun batchUpdate(actors: List<Actor>): IntArray {\n\t\treturn this.namedParameterJdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = :firstName, last_name = :lastName where id = :id\",\n\t\t\t\tSqlParameterSourceUtils.createBatch(actors));\n\t}\n\n\t\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "For an SQL statement that uses the classic "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "?"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " placeholders, you pass in a list containing an object array with the update values. This object array must have one entry for each placeholder in the SQL statement, and they must be in the same order as they are defined in the SQL statement."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example is the same as the preceding example, except that it uses classic JDBC "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "?"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " placeholders:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "public class JdbcActorDao implements ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;\n\n\tpublic void setDataSource(DataSource dataSource) {\n\t\tthis.jdbcTemplate = new JdbcTemplate(dataSource);\n\t}\n\n\tpublic int[] batchUpdate(final List<Actor> actors) {\n\t\tList<Object[]> batch = new ArrayList<>();\n\t\tfor (Actor actor : actors) {\n\t\t\tObject[] values = new Object[] {\n\t\t\t\t\tactor.getFirstName(), actor.getLastName(), actor.getId()};\n\t\t\tbatch.add(values);\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn this.jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = ?, last_name = ? where id = ?\",\n\t\t\t\tbatch);\n\t}\n\n\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "class JdbcActorDao(dataSource: DataSource) : ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate val jdbcTemplate = JdbcTemplate(dataSource)\n\n\tfun batchUpdate(actors: List<Actor>): IntArray {\n\t\tval batch = mutableListOf<Array<Any>>()\n\t\tfor (actor in actors) {\n\t\t\tbatch.add(arrayOf(actor.firstName, actor.lastName, actor.id))\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = ?, last_name = ? where id = ?\", batch)\n\t}\n\n\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "All of the batch update methods that we described earlier return an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "int"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " array containing the number of affected rows for each batch entry. This count is reported by the JDBC driver. If the count is not available, the JDBC driver returns a value of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-2"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "In such a scenario, with automatic setting of values on an underlying "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "PreparedStatement"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ", the corresponding JDBC type for each value needs to be derived from the given Java type. While this usually works well, there is a potential for issues (for example, with Map-contained "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "null"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " values). Spring, by default, calls "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ParameterMetaData.getParameterType"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " in such a case, which can be expensive with your JDBC driver. You should use a recent driver version and consider setting the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "spring.jdbc.getParameterType.ignore"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " property to "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "true"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " (as a JVM system property or via the "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "SpringProperties"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "appendix.html#appendix-spring-properties"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " mechanism) if you encounter a specific performance issue for your application."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "As of 6.1.2, Spring bypasses the default "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "getParameterType"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " resolution on PostgreSQL and MS SQL Server. This is a common optimization to avoid further roundtrips to the DBMS just for parameter type resolution which is known to make a very significant difference on PostgreSQL and MS SQL Server specifically, in particular for batch operations. If you happen to see a side effect, for example, when setting a byte array to null without specific type indication, you may explicitly set the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "spring.jdbc.getParameterType.ignore=false"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " flag as a system property (see above) to restore full "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "getParameterType"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " resolution."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Alternatively, you could consider specifying the corresponding JDBC types explicitly, either through a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "BatchPreparedStatementSetter"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " (as shown earlier), through an explicit type array given to a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "List<Object[]>"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " based call, through "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "registerSqlType"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " calls on a custom "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "MapSqlParameterSource"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " instance, through a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "BeanPropertySqlParameterSource"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " that derives the SQL type from the Java-declared property type even for a null value, or through providing individual "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "SqlParameterValue"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " instances instead of plain null values."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jdbc-batch-list",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Batch Operations with a List of Objects"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The preceding example of a batch update deals with batches that are so large that you want to break them up into several smaller batches. You can do this with the methods mentioned earlier by making multiple calls to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "batchUpdate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method, but there is now a more convenient method. This method takes, in addition to the SQL statement, a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Collection"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " of objects that contain the parameters, the number of updates to make for each batch, and a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ParameterizedPreparedStatementSetter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to set the values for the parameters of the prepared statement. The framework loops over the provided values and breaks the update calls into batches of the size specified."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example shows a batch update that uses a batch size of 100:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "public class JdbcActorDao implements ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;\n\n\tpublic void setDataSource(DataSource dataSource) {\n\t\tthis.jdbcTemplate = new JdbcTemplate(dataSource);\n\t}\n\n\tpublic int[][] batchUpdate(final Collection<Actor> actors) {\n\t\tint[][] updateCounts = jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = ?, last_name = ? where id = ?\",\n\t\t\t\tactors,\n\t\t\t\t100,\n\t\t\t\t(PreparedStatement ps, Actor actor) -> {\n\t\t\t\t\tps.setString(1, actor.getFirstName());\n\t\t\t\t\tps.setString(2, actor.getLastName());\n\t\t\t\t\tps.setLong(3, actor.getId().longValue());\n\t\t\t\t});\n\t\treturn updateCounts;\n\t}\n\n\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "class JdbcActorDao(dataSource: DataSource) : ActorDao {\n\n\tprivate val jdbcTemplate = JdbcTemplate(dataSource)\n\n\tfun batchUpdate(actors: List<Actor>): Array<IntArray> {\n\t\treturn jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(\n\t\t\t\t\t\"update t_actor set first_name = ?, last_name = ? where id = ?\",\n\t\t\t\t\tactors, 100) { ps, argument ->\n\t\t\tps.setString(1, argument.firstName)\n\t\t\tps.setString(2, argument.lastName)\n\t\t\tps.setLong(3, argument.id)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// ... additional methods\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The batch update method for this call returns an array of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "int"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " arrays that contains an array entry for each batch with an array of the number of affected rows for each update. The top-level array’s length indicates the number of batches run, and the second level array’s length indicates the number of updates in that batch. The number of updates in each batch should be the batch size provided for all batches (except that the last one that might be less), depending on the total number of update objects provided. The update count for each update statement is the one reported by the JDBC driver. If the count is not available, the JDBC driver returns a value of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-2"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jdbc-batch-multi",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Batch Operations with Multiple Batches"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
